      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الْمَرْأَةِ عَلَيْهَا أَذَانٌ وَ إِقَامَةٌ قَالَ لَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin Sh<span class=\"iTxt\">Azān</span>, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Jameel Bin Darraj who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the woman, ‘Is there a recitation of an <span class=\"iTxt\">Azān</span> and an <span class=\"iTxt\">Iqamah</span> upon her?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "18. Muhammad ibn ’Isma‘il has narrated from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Jamil ibn Darraj who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, if a woman is required to say Adhan and ‘Iqamah. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, she is not required.’” "
        ]
      }
